|366016|6133799003|10067099003|22082099003|18002099003|8096899003|13003099007|38070700021|261021123027099003|56012099006|261021121427099003|4143699003|11063799006|261022075727099003|261028144727099003|261102123227099003|261026140227099003|261026121527099003|261009223027099003|261022105027099003;\nL29: x-microsoft-antispam-message-info: \nL30: x-forefront-antispam-report: CIP:255.255.255.255;CTRY:;LANG:en;SCL:1;SRV:;IPV:NLI;SFV:NSPM;H:BYAPR13MB4311.namprd13.prod.outlook.com;PTR:;CAT:NONE;SFS:(13230040)(4022899009)(23010399003)(376014)(1800799024)(366016)(6133799003)(10067099003)(22082099003)(18002099003)(8096899003)(13003099007)(38070700021)(261021123027099003)(56012099006)(261021121427099003)(4143699003)(11063799006)(261022075727099003)(261028144727099003)(261102123227099003)(261026140227099003)(261026121527099003)(261009223027099003)(261022105027099003);DIR:OUT;SFP:1102;\nL31: x-ms-exchange-antispam-messagedata-chunkcount: 1\nL32: x-ms-exchange-antispam-messagedata-0: \nL33: Content-Type: multipart/alternative; boundary=\"_000_BYAPR13MB431137436640A04456BB8C4885692BYAPR13MB4311namp_\"\nL34: MIME-Version: 1.0\nL35: X-OriginatorOrg: Futurewei.com\nL36: X-MS-Exchange-CrossTenant-AuthAs: Internal\nL37: X-MS-Exchange-CrossTenant-AuthSource: BYAPR13MB4311.namprd13.prod.outlook.com\nL38: X-MS-Exchange-CrossTenant-Network-Message-Id: 8c87e58f-5c37-4ffc-635a-08df39efd2a5\nL39: X-MS-Exchange-CrossTenant-originalarrivaltime: 03 Nov 2026 21:17:10.3498 (UTC)\nL40: X-MS-Exchange-CrossTenant-fromentityheader: Hosted\nL41: X-MS-Exchange-CrossTenant-id: 0fee8ff2-a3b2-4018-9c75-3a1d5591fedc\nL42: X-MS-Exchange-CrossTenant-mailboxtype: HOSTED\nL43: X-MS-Exchange-CrossTenant-userprincipalname: 0abFoxjfK7nqFH3SYMg0wyoeUTa/mKu+Cg5p/xl98DhRPM0aw0Wo8KhgaVFh8cUOA+Z/VpsIRtdb7OKN0t7KpQ==\nL44: X-MS-Exchange-Transport-CrossTenantHeadersStamped: FT1PR13MB994406\nL45: X-Spamd-Bar: ------------------------\nL46: Message-ID-Hash: ONYXYMTDHE73M6YDFSIM7TFXVANTGFOL\nL47: X-Message-ID-Hash: ONYXYMTDHE73M6YDFSIM7TFXVANTGFOL\nL48: X-MailFrom: linda.dunbar@futurewei.com\nL49: X-Mailman-Rule-Misses: dmarc-mitigation; no-senders; approved; loop; banned-address; emergency; member-moderation; nonmember-moderation; administrivia; implicit-dest; max-recipients; max-size; news-moderation; no-subject; digests; suspicious-header\nL50: X-Mailman-Version: 3.3.10\nL51: Precedence: list\nL52: Subject: [Dawn] Re: Updated draft-dunbar-dawn-infra-assisted-discovery\nL53: List-Id: \"The list is for discussion of the scope, use cases, requirements, and solutions for discovery of entities (e.g., tasks, AI agents, or endpoints) using IETF technologies.\" <dawn.ietf.org>\nL54: Archived-At: <https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/msg/dawn/6m1_jcurI0F0_LadffO71f0d4m8>\nL55: List-Archive: <https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/browse/dawn>\nL56: List-Help: <mailto:dawn-request@ietf.org?subject=help>\nL57: List-Owner: <mailto:dawn-owner@ietf.org>\nL58: List-Post: <mailto:dawn@ietf.org>\nL59: List-Subscribe: <mailto:dawn-join@ietf.org>\nL60: List-Unsubscribe: <mailto:dawn-leave@ietf.org>\nL61: \nL62:     Aleksandr,\nL63: \nL64:     Thanks. I agree they are complementary.\nL65: \nL66:     Per the DAWN charter, the discovered AI resource may itself be a service such as a catalog that furthers the discovery process. So bootstrap discovery can return the minimum public information needed to reach such a catalog.\nL67:     I would still keep the metadata reference resource-specific, e.g., pointing to an Agent Card. Catalog search, capability comparison, ranking, or selection after reaching the catalog remain outside the bootstrap scope.\nL68: \nL69:     Best regards,\nL70:     Linda\nL71: \nL72:     From: Александр Артамохов <alexar76=40rambler.ru@dmarc.ietf.org>\nL73:     Sent: Saturday, October 31, 2026 10:51 PM\nL74:     To: adrian@olddog.co.uk; dawn@ietf.org; Linda Dunbar <linda.dunbar@futurewei.com>\nL75:     Subject: RE: [Dawn] Updated draft-dunbar-dawn-infra-assisted-discovery\nL76: \nL77:     Hi Linda,\nL78: \nL79:     Thank's for the update.\nL80: \nL81:     The clear boundary in -03 is helpful: bootstrap discovery returns the minimum needed to reach an agent, while catalog search, ranking and cost-based selection stay out of scope.\nL82:     That excluded part is what draft-artamokhov-dawn-marketplace-discovery addresses: how a requester finds catalogs (marketplaces) that list agents and tools across operators, through a well-known URI, before any selection happens.\nL83:     The two seem complementary: your model finds an entry point inside a managed network, and a catalog is used when the requester has to search beyond it.\nL84:     One question: should the metadata reference returned by bootstrap discovery be allowed to point to such a catalog, or do you see catalogs as entirely separate from bootstrap discovery?\nL85: \nL86:     Best regards, Aleksandr Artamokhov\nL87: \nL88:     01.11.2026, 05:47, Linda Dunbar <linda.dunbar=40futurewei.com@dmarc.ietf.org<mailto:linda.dunbar=40futurewei.com@dmarc.ietf.org>>\nL89:     Hi all,\nL90: \nL91:     Thanks to Adrian for the detailed comments, and to everyone for the helpful discussion on the DAWN mailing list.\nL92:     We have updated draft 【0†https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-dunbar-dawn-infra-assisted-discovery/†datatracker.ietf.org】 . The revision aligns the terminology more closely with the DAWN terminology draft, in particular around MVD/MDI and the role of requester context.\nL93: It also clarifies that the infrastructure-assisted model supports bootstrap discovery by contributing current resource state and requester context, without defining registration, catalog search, semantic matchmaking, ranking, or resource selection.\nL94: \nL95:     The updated draft also distinguishes more clearly between DAWN bootstrap discovery and subsequent retrieval of richer agent-native metadata such as an A2A Agent Card.\nL96: \nL97:     Comments and suggestions are very welcome.\nL98: \nL99:     Best regards,\nL100:     Linda\nL101: \nL102: \nL103: \nL104: \nL105: \nL106: \nL107: \nL108: \nL109: \nL110: \nL111: \nL112: \nL113: \nL114: \nL115: \nL116: \nL117: \nL118: \nL119: \nL120: \nL121: \nL122: \nL123: \nL124:     _______________________________________________\nL125:     Dawn mailing list -- dawn@ietf.org</compose>\nL126:     To unsubscribe send an email to dawn-leave@ietf.org</compose>\nL127:   * 【1†[Dawn] Updated draft-dunbar-dawn-infra-assisted-d…】  Linda Dunbar\nL128:   * 【2†[Dawn] Re: Updated draft-dunbar-dawn-infra-assist…】  Александр Артамохов\nL129:   * 【3†[Dawn] Re: Updated draft-dunbar-dawn-infra-assist…】  Girish Konda\nL130:   * 【4†[Dawn] Re: Updated draft-dunbar-dawn-infra-assist…】  Linda Dunbar\nL131:   * 【5†[Dawn] Re: Updated draft-dunbar-dawn-infra-assist…】  Linda Dunbar\nL132:   * 【6†[Dawn] Re: Updated draft-dunbar-dawn-infra-assist…】  Girish Konda\nL133: \nL134:   * 【7†Hide Navigation Bar】\nL135: \nL136: Date\nL137: \nL138: Thread\nL139: v2.46.0 | 【8†Report a Bug†github.com】 | By Email (tools-help@ietf.org) | 【9†System Status†status.ietf.org】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn82view1 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://lupariel.com/fichas/aimarket-hub/\",\"lineno\":null}); \nFailed to fetch https://lupariel.com/fichas/aimarket-hub/: Cache miss--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn82view2 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://1gateway.dev/market/modelmarket.dev\",\"lineno\":null}); \nFailed to fetch https://1gateway.dev/market/modelmarket.dev: Cache miss"
